
# GITHUB ACTIONS

## GitHub Actions

- GitHub Actions lets me automate tasks when things happen in my repository.

- For example:

    Push code
        ↓
    GitHub Action runs
        ↓
    Tests run
        ↓
    Code is checked

- Actions can be used for:

    - Running tests
    - Linting
    - Building applications
    - Deploying websites
    - Creating releases
    - Checking security
    - Automating repetitive tasks

- GitHub Actions uses workflow files, normally stored in:

    .github/workflows/

- Example:

    .github/
        workflows/
            tests.yml

