# CI/CD

## Continuous Integration

- Continuous Integration (CI) means automatically checking code as developers make changes.

- For example:

    Developer pushes code
        ↓
    Tests automatically run
        ↓
    Tests pass/fail
        ↓
    Developers know whether something broke

- CI helps catch bugs early.

---

## Continuous Deployment

- Continuous Deployment (CD) can automatically deploy code after it passes checks.

- Example:

    Push code
        ↓
    Tests
        ↓
    Build
        ↓
    Deploy

- This can be used to automatically update a live website.

